# The read must FAIL: Surelog reports the seventeen ILLEGAL lines in dut.sv --
# enum members with a non-constant value (CP0359), an x/z value in a 2-state
# base (CP0355, twice), no value after an x/z member (CP0356), a value the
# base cannot hold (CP0357, three times), an invalid base type (CP0358,
# twice), a module instantiated in a program (CP0361), a zero replication outside a concatenation (CP0362), an
# inout port default (CP0363), a reg on an inout port or tran terminal
# (UH0751, twice), an unassignable inout actual or assign target (UH0752,
# twice) and a procedural write to a wire array element (UH0718).  The exact
# count pins it to those: x in a 4-state enum, a based literal that fills an
# int, a parameter-width base, nets on a switch, a concatenation on an inout,
# a zero replication beside real bits and a nested generate region must stay
# silent.
logger -expect error "Surelog reported 0 fatal, 0 syntax and 17 other error" 1
read_sv -nonote -noinfo -nowarning dut.sv
